@startuml components-swing-conditional
' SplitSmart - Conditional Swing alternative [COND-B]
' Valid ONLY with documented customer approval (OQ-1). Does NOT satisfy NFR-001 / AC-020.
' Sources: architecture.md section 3.2; contracts/ui-workflows.md section 6; decisions.md D-02.
title SplitSmart - Components (Alternative B: Swing desktop) [CONDITIONAL - NFR-001 NOT met]

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle uml2

actor "Account holders\n(same computer)" as Users

rectangle "Single desktop installation" {
  package "splitsmart.desktop [COND-B]" {
    [Swing views (EDT only)] as Views
    [Presenters (no javax.swing)] as Pres
    [SessionHolder] as Sess
    [DesktopApplication\n(composition root)] as Root
  }
  package "splitsmart.application (same as A)" {
    [Application services +\nAuthorizationService + AuditRecorder] as Svc
  }
  package "splitsmart.domain (same as A)" {
    [Domain rules] as Dom
  }
  package "splitsmart.persistence (same as A)" {
    [JPA repositories + Flyway] as Repo
  }
  database "Embedded H2 file\n(user profile dir)" as H2
}

Users --> Views
Views --> Pres : events
Pres --> Views : view-models
Pres --> Svc : SwingWorker calls
Pres --> Sess
Svc --> Dom
Svc --> Repo : via ports
Repo --> H2
Root ..> Pres : wires
Root ..> Svc : wires

note bottom of H2
  Recovery uses one-time codes (no email).
  Notifications are visible only on this machine.
  File readable by OS users unless encrypted.
end note
@enduml
